AUDIO: 'What you\'re looking at is a stunning Gaussian&nbsp; Splatting scene. Which is captured using the&nbsp;&nbsp; Antigravity A1 drone and processed using MipMap&nbsp; software. And the best part? With native 360&nbsp;&nbsp; camera support in MipMap 3D reconstruction&nbsp; software, creating Gaussian Splats using a&nbsp;&nbsp; panoramic drone is now as easy as using a standard&nbsp; drone. The processing workflow in this video&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:16] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: MipMap 3.0 splash screen focusing on 360 Camera Support for Insta360 and DJI Osmo 360.
AUDIO: 'also applies when using Insta360 and DJI Osmo&nbsp; 360 cameras. Usually, to get a good Gaussian&nbsp;&nbsp; Splatting result, a standard drone has to capture&nbsp; images from different directions. This makes&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:30] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A 360-degree fisheye view of a scene, demonstrating the wide field of view.
AUDIO: 'data collection incredibly slow and significantly&nbsp; increases your training time. But a 360 panoramic&nbsp;&nbsp; drone changes the game. With dual fisheye lenses&nbsp; offering over 180 degrees of field-of-view, just&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:42] [scene:demo]
VISUAL: A 360-degree fisheye view of a scene, demonstrating the wide field of view.
AUDIO: 'the bottom lens alone captures all the angles you&nbsp; need, massively boosting your efficiency. However,&nbsp;&nbsp; most Gaussian Splatting software out there can\'t&nbsp; handle raw panoramic drone data. You usually have&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:55] [scene:explanation]
VISUAL: Diagram showing how a 360 panoramic view is divided into standard perspectives (North, East, South, West). MipMap 3.0 splash screen highlighting 360 Camera Support, Fisheye Support, and other features.
AUDIO: 'to chop it up and pre-process it across multiple&nbsp; programs, which is a huge, error-prone headache.&nbsp;&nbsp; With MipMap 3.0. We\'ve added native support&nbsp; for 360 panoramic videos. You can directly&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:07] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: MipMap 3.0 splash screen highlighting 360 Camera Support, Fisheye Support, and other features.
AUDIO: 'import raw data from Insta360, DJI Osmo 360, and&nbsp; the Antigravity A1 for one-click reconstruction.&nbsp;&nbsp; Let’s take a look at how simple this workflow&nbsp; really is.if you haven’t installed MipMap yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:22] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: MipMap 3.0 task parameters interface, showing options for task type, photos, aerial triangulation, and reconstruction settings.
AUDIO: 'click the video link in the top right corner to&nbsp; check out our complete Quick Start Guide! First,&nbsp;&nbsp; create a new task in MipMap and click \'Import&nbsp; Video\'. Select your video straight from the&nbsp;&nbsp; drone’s SD card—no third-party prep required.&nbsp; Next, set your frame extraction interval. For&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:38] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: MipMap 3.0 showing "Extracting frames..." progress.
AUDIO: 'Gaussian Splatting, you want an 80 to 90 percent&nbsp; overlap between adjacent frames. But remember,&nbsp;&nbsp; too many photos will significantly increase your&nbsp; reconstruction time. You can check the overlap&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:50] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: MipMap 3.0 displaying photo info with a 360-degree image preview.
AUDIO: 'rate after extraction and adjust the interval if&nbsp; needed. Here\'s a quick pro-tip for the Antigravity&nbsp;&nbsp; A1: since the top lens mostly just films the sky,&nbsp; it doesn\'t help our scene and can actually cause&nbsp;&nbsp; floaters and increase processing time. We can just&nbsp; go ahead and delete that camera view entirely. If&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:08] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: MipMap 3.0 showing "Extracting frames..." progress.
AUDIO: 'you have multiple videos of the same scene, simply&nbsp; import them and repeat these steps. Once your data&nbsp;&nbsp; is loaded, click the camera settings icon. MipMap&nbsp; comes pre-loaded with parameters for Insta and&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:20] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: MipMap 3.0 camera settings interface, showing options for perspective, fisheye, focal length, and distortion parameters. MipMap 3.0 task parameters interface after camera settings are saved.
AUDIO: 'DJI cameras. For the Antigravity A1, simply select&nbsp; the \'Insta X5 8K\' camera profile. Finally, select&nbsp;&nbsp; \'Ultra High\' precision and turn the Gaussian&nbsp; Splatting toggle ON. To save processing time,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:37] [scene:ui]
